  Act as an ontology engineer. Use the following content (examples, part of the ontology, and a list of guidelines) as a guide to translate the natural language rule you are given into a SWRL rule. 
  EXAMPLES
    Example 1
    Rule in natural language: If a person has a sibling who is a man, then the person has a brother.
    SWRL rule: Person(?p) ^ hasSibling(?p, ?s) ^ Person(?s) ^ IsMan(?s, true) -> hasBrother(?p, ?s)

    Example 2
    Rule in natural language: if a person has a phone number that starts with '+', then the person has an international phone number.
    SWRL rule: Person(?p) ^ hasPhoneNumber(?p, ?number) ^ swrlb:startsWith(?number, "+") -> hasInternationalPhoneNumber(?p, true)

    Example 3
    Rule in natural language:  if a person has age greater than 17, then the person is an adult and has id card.
    SWRL rule: Person(?p) ^ hasAge(?p, ?age) ^ Age(?age) ^ swrlb:greaterThan(?age, 17) ^ IdCard(?id) -> Adult(?p) ^ hasIdCard(?p, ?id)

    Example 4
    Rule in natural language: if a publication has two different authors, then those authors have cooperated with each other.
    SWRL rule: Publication(?p) ^ Author(?y) ^ Author(?z) ^ hasAuthor(?p, ?y) ^ hasAuthor(?p, ?z) ^ differentFrom(?y, ?z) -> cooperatedWith(?y, ?z)

    Example 5
    Rule in natural language: if a researcher has published more than 10 papers in a Top-Tier conference, then the researcher is a prominent researcher and has a high citation impact.
    SWRL rule: Researcher(?r) ^ hasPublished(?r, ?c) ^ Conference(?c) ^ topTierConference(?c) ^ swrlb:greaterThan(count(?c), 10) -> ProminentResearcher(?r) ^ hasHighCitationImpact(?r, true)
  END OF EXAMPLES
  PART OF ONTOLOGY 
    ###  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beAWARE-project/ontology/master/beAWARE_ontology#isClimateParameterOfIncident
beAWARE_ontology:isClimateParameterOfIncident rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                              rdfs:domain beAWARE_ontology:ClimateParameter ;
                                              rdfs:range beAWARE_ontology:Incident ;
                                              rdfs:label "is climate parameter of incident" ;
                                              skos:definition "Links a climate parameter measurement to an incident." .
###  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beAWARE-project/ontology/master/beAWARE_ontology#hasIncidentClimateParameter
beAWARE_ontology:hasIncidentClimateParameter rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                             owl:inverseOf beAWARE_ontology:isClimateParameterOfIncident ;
                                             rdfs:domain beAWARE_ontology:Incident ;
                                             rdfs:range beAWARE_ontology:ClimateParameter ;
                                             rdfs:label "has incident climate parameter" ;
                                             skos:definition "Associates an incident to a climate parameter measurement." .
###  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beAWARE-project/ontology/master/beAWARE_ontology#hasMeasurementLocation
beAWARE_ontology:hasMeasurementLocation rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                        owl:inverseOf beAWARE_ontology:isLocationOfMeasurement ;
                                        rdfs:domain beAWARE_ontology:ClimateParameter ;
                                        rdfs:range beAWARE_ontology:Location ;
                                        rdfs:label "has measurement location" ;
                                        skos:definition "Represents the location where a climate parameter measurement was taken." .
###  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beAWARE-project/ontology/master/beAWARE_ontology#hasClimateParameterMeasurement
beAWARE_ontology:hasClimateParameterMeasurement rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                owl:inverseOf beAWARE_ontology:relatesToNaturalDisaster ;
                                                rdfs:domain beAWARE_ontology:NaturalDisaster ;
                                                rdfs:range beAWARE_ontology:ClimateParameter ;
                                                rdfs:label "has disaster climate parameter" ;
                                                skos:definition "Associates a natural disaster occurrence to a climate parameter measurement." .
###  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beAWARE-project/ontology/master/beAWARE_ontology#isLocationOfMeasurement
beAWARE_ontology:isLocationOfMeasurement rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                         rdfs:domain beAWARE_ontology:Location ;
                                         rdfs:range beAWARE_ontology:ClimateParameter ;
                                         rdfs:label "is location of measurement" ;
                                         skos:definition "Links a location to a climate parameter measurement." .
###  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beAWARE-project/ontology/master/beAWARE_ontology#isLocationOfIncident
beAWARE_ontology:isLocationOfIncident rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                      rdfs:domain beAWARE_ontology:Location ;
                                      rdfs:range beAWARE_ontology:Incident ;
                                      rdfs:label "is location of incident" ;
                                      skos:definition "Links a location to an incident occurrence." .
###  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/beAWARE-project/ontology/master/beAWARE_ontology#hasClimateParameterOccurrence
beAWARE_ontology:hasClimateParameterOccurrence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                               owl:inverseOf beAWARE_ontology:isOfClimateParameterType ;
                                               rdfs:domain beAWARE_ontology:ClimateParameterType ;
                                               rdfs:range beAWARE_ontology:ClimateParameter ;
                                               rdfs:label "has climate parameter occurrence" ;
                                               skos:definition "Assigns a climate parameter type to a specific climate parameter." .
  END OF ONTOLOGY

  COMMON GUIDELINES

  Please try to implement the following guidelines:
  1: Variables e.g., (?something) used in Conclusions must be present in Conditions. So create as many variables as needed in Conditions. 
  2: Each atom must have exactly one variable if it represents class.
  3: Each atom must have exactly two variables if it represents object property.
  4: Each concept must be represented by a class and must be present in Conditions.

  END OF COMMON GUIDELINES

  The rule in natural language is the following: If a measurement of a climate parameter is taken at a specific location, and an incident occurs at that same location, then that measurement can be associated with that incident.
